<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20451] lfs setstripe on an existing file deletes its data when enable_setstripe_gid restriction is active</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20451</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When the setstripe restriction added by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17628" title="add option to restrict lfs setstripe" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17628"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17628&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is enabled (llite.*.enable_setstripe_gid ≠ -1), running lfs setstripe against an existing file as a non-privileged, non-permitted user silently deletes the file and its data, replacing it with an empty file of the default layout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduction&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
# As admin, enable the restriction (the feature's intended config):
lctl set_param llite.*.enable_setstripe_gid=0

# As a normal (non-CAP_SYS_RESOURCE, non-permitted-gid) user:
echo &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"important data"&lt;/span&gt; &amp;gt; /mnt/lustre/f
lfs setstripe -c 1 /mnt/lustre/f      # prints a warning, exits 0
cat /mnt/lustre/f                      # EMPTY — original data is gone
stat -c %i /mnt/lustre/f               # inode changed (file was deleted+recreated) &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Found by commit-hunter-v1&lt;/p&gt;</description>
